format session-log-v1
stamp 20260821.192038
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The manual's other rooms read, and a reference that corrected mine
prompt read the manual's other rooms too
think Reused last round's method with the correction it taught -- resolve every cited path from its citing file rather than from the root, and read the surrounding line before calling a miss a break.
think That correction paid immediately. Twenty-six apparent path misses shrank to two real ones once labels, placeholders, and shapes were told apart. Three were link labels whose targets were correct beside them; several were gitignored files a reader creates; one was a session-log SHAPE written as YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS_slug, which is the naming law being quoted properly rather than a path.
think Checked tool existence separately from command shape, because a path that exists says nothing about whether the command around it can run. Thirty-four tools named across the rooms, thirty-two real, and both missing ones are files the reader is told to create two lines earlier.
think Found the bare-invocation fault twice more, and in the worst place it could be: two VIDEO SCRIPTS put a bare rye build on screen under an ON-SCREEN marker as a command that types itself and completes. A wrong command in a guide costs a reader a minute; the same command in a video costs everyone who watches, and cannot be corrected in their copy.
think Named why that class survives: the further a page is from a terminal, the less it is tested. A video script is never executed, only performed, so nothing catches it -- and it reaches the most people.
think Widened the existing guard rather than adding a third, since both checks are one concern: a page telling a reader something untrue about the tools a clone carries. The line between defect and legitimate use turned out to be mechanical, which is the only reason it is checkable -- runnable blocks are fenced bash or sh, while usage tables and captured version output sit in unlabeled fences.
think Went into the reference room expecting the rival-first-hour pattern again, since a second Rishi reference now exists and the elder one pledges it documents only what runs. Tested its specific claims rather than assuming mine superseded it.
think Was wrong, and gladly. Every claim I tested on manual/reference/rishi-language.md held -- including .len on lists and strings, and flag args --name, BOTH of which my new field guide had missed. A reference checked against the language was corrected by a reference checked against the language.
think Read section 15, Named Gaps, expecting stale claims from seven weeks ago, and found it does not list missing features at all. It names the witness backing each feature and says new surface enters only on the day its witness runs green. A correct, well-aged sentence.
obs Resolved the duplication as a pair rather than a winner, the same way the two first-hour pages were resolved. The elder is the CONFORMANCE reference -- fifteen numbered sections, must and should carrying their weight, pinned at parity 142. Mine is the FIELD GUIDE -- what to reach for, and the seven edges the contract does not name. A language wants both.
obs Two stale references were repointed rather than resolved, per the mark law: living things are repointed. Both had moved to yonder and to crux/archive -- judgement moves the fold rule cannot predict, so the repointer correctly left them and a hand was needed. Worth naming as the repointer's honest boundary.
obs My probe of flag used the wrong shape and the interpreter named the fault exactly -- FlagNeedsName. A good error message is a reference too.
loom review=manual_rooms files=26 paths_checked=26 real_breaks=2 tools_named=34 tools_real=32 placeholders=2
loom defects=bare_invocation found=2 place=video_scripts corrected=2 build_verified=yes
loom reference=elder claims_tested=4 held=4 gaps_in_mine=2 dot_len=works flag_two_arg=works
file manual/video-scripts/first-module-walkthrough.md the on-screen command a viewer could not run
file manual/video-scripts/intro-what-is-grain.md the same, in the introduction people watch first
file manual/guides/macos-ai-jail-setup.md repointed to the yonder home
file manual/guides/cloud-agent-toolchain-setup.md repointed to the crux archive home
file manual/reference/rishi-language.md the field guide named beside the contract
file docs-geode/api/rishi-language-reference.md .len and flag added -- the elder reference's corrections
file tools/fixtures/shipped_binary_claim_scan.sh a second check beside the first, same concern
file crux/REDS.md %119 -- a command typed on camera, and the happier half
recommend check-in (checkpoint) the manual is read end to end now -- five guides last round, twenty-six pages this one -- and both classes it surfaced are guarded. The honest remaining gap is the one no guard reaches: a claim about BEHAVIOR rather than about a name or a path, which only a reader's full walk would test. That is a real round rather than a lap, and worth its own word.
